    "body": "Hello,\r\nI came across a surprising crash with supernova and I traced it down to running multiple SendTrig UGens in a Parallel Group. I'm on the recent develop build on macOS 10.12.\r\nThe following will crash on my machine after few triggers of SendTrig (I assume this indeterminacy is because the synths are started asynchronously). I would really appreciate if others confirmed this happening on different systems as well. Reproducer:\r\n\r\n```\r\nServer.supernova;\r\ns.boot;\r\n\r\n(\r\nfork{\r\n\t~mainGroup = ParGroup.new;\r\n\t// ~mainGroup = Group.new; //doesn't crash in a regular group\r\n\ts.sync;\r\n\t~def = OSCdef(\\update, {|msg| postf(\"id: %, time: %\\n\", msg[2], msg[3].round(0.01))}, '/tr'); //post triggers to see progress\r\n\t~trigSynths = 4.collect({|doInc| //crash happens for me with 3 and more SendTrig synths\r\n\t\t{SendTrig.kr(Impulse.kr(4), doInc, Sweep.kr)}.play(target: ~mainGroup); //the faster the impulse, the sooner the crash happens\r\n\t});\r\n}\r\n)\r\n\r\n~trigSynths.do(_.free); ~def.free;\r\n```",
