      "body": "Confirmed -- it crashes very quickly for me in Ubuntu Studio 16.04, 3.9 beta branch.\r\n\r\nI'll take a guess that the SendTrig UGen code assumes it could never possibly be constructing multiple outgoing messages at the same time.\r\n\r\nHowever, SendReply is unaffected -- I'm running the test code now with the following substitution:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\t\t{SendReply.kr(Impulse.kr(4), '/tr', doInc, Sweep.kr)}.play(target: ~mainGroup);\r\n```\r\n\r\n... and it's up to `id: 50` and counting, no crash.\r\n\r\nOf course SendTrig should be fixed, but there is a workaround: use SendReply.\r\n\r\n(TBH, SendReply is more flexible -- I don't understand why anybody is still using SendTrig. IMO SendTrig may be a candidate for deprecation.)",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
